# Command yamllint

## What does this command do:

YAML linter — checks syntax validity plus cosmetic issues: indentation, line length, trailing spaces, key ordering, duplicate keys, and truthy value style

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: `pip install --user yamllint`

To upgrade: `pip install --user --upgrade yamllint`

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/yamllint

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://yamllint.readthedocs.io/en/stable/

## Command options

# --- Basic usage ---

# Lint a single file
yamllint file.yaml

# Lint all YAML files in a directory (recursive)
yamllint .

# Lint from stdin
cat file.yaml | yamllint -

# --- Output formats ---

# Standard (default) — human readable with rule names
yamllint -f standard file.yaml

# Colored output
yamllint -f colored file.yaml

# Parsable (for editors / CI tools)
yamllint -f parsable file.yaml

# GitHub Actions annotations
yamllint -f github file.yaml

# --- Strictness ---

# Strict mode: warnings become errors (exit 1 on warnings too)
yamllint -s file.yaml

# Suppress warnings, show errors only
yamllint --no-warnings file.yaml

# --- Config ---

# Use a specific config file
yamllint -c .yamllint.yaml file.yaml

# Use a built-in profile: default | relaxed
yamllint -d relaxed file.yaml

# Pass config inline (overrides .yamllint)
yamllint -d '{extends: default, rules: {line-length: {max: 120}}}' file.yaml

# --- .yamllint config file (place in project root) ---
# extends: default
# rules:
#   line-length:
#     max: 120
#   truthy:
#     allowed-values: ['true', 'false']
#     check-keys: false
#   comments:
#     min-spaces-from-content: 1
#   indentation:
#     spaces: 2
#     indent-sequences: true

# --- List files that would be linted ---
yamllint --list-files .

# --- Check version ---
yamllint --version

# --- CI one-liner (lint all YAML, fail on warnings) ---
find . -name '*.yml' -o -name '*.yaml' | xargs yamllint -s
